<article class="english-guide"><nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/en/">English home</a> / <span>Reading guide</span></nav><header><p class="eyebrow">ENGLISH READER'S LIBRARY · JOSÉ HERNÁNDEZ</p><h1>Martín Fierro Summary: Plot, Characters, and the Two Parts</h1><p class="deck">What happens in Martín Fierro? José Hernández tells a gaucho's story in two connected poems: first the destruction of his settled life, then the difficult question of how to live after loss. Here is a guide to the plot without confusing the narrator with the author.</p></header><figure class="hero"><img src="/media/fotografias-v3/la-ida.webp" width="1200" height="720" alt="Editorial illustration of a gaucho traveling across the Argentine pampas" fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption>Modern digital reconstruction; not a historical photograph.</figcaption></figure><div class="body"><nav class="toc" aria-label="Contents"><strong>On this page</strong>{sections.map(s=><a href={`#${s.id}`}>{s.heading}</a>)}<a href="#sources">Sources</a></nav>{sections.map((s,i)=><><section id={s.id}><h2>{s.heading}</h2>{s.paragraphs.map(p=><p>{p}</p>)}</section>{i===0&&<AdSlot id="article-02-after-introduction" kind="article"/>}{i===2&&<AdSlot id="article-03-middle" kind="article"/>}{i===4&&<AdSlot id="article-04-before-references" kind="article"/>}</>)}<section id="sources"><h2>Historical sources and further reading</h2><p>This guide provides original English explanation, not an English transcription of the poem. Publication history, literary interpretation and modern editorial illustration are distinguished.</p><ul>{sources.map(s=><li><a href={s.url} target={s.url.startsWith('https:')?'_blank':undefined} rel={s.url.startsWith('https:')?'noopener noreferrer':undefined}>{s.name}</a></li>)}</ul><p><a href="/en/characters/">Characters</a> · <a href="/en/what-is-a-gaucho/">Gaucho history</a> · <a href="/en/magazine/">Cultural magazine</a></p></section><AdSlot id="article-05-after-article" kind="article"/></div></article>
